#: ../../../techref/justification_codes.md:5
msgid "Justification Codes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/justification_codes.md:7
msgid ""
"To place plot embellishments, such as scalebars, directional roses, "
"colorbars, legends, text, or images on a plot, two points have to be "
"specified: a point somewhere on the figure (**reference point**) and a point "
"on the feature (**anchor point**). For both, users can use a two-character "
"code, a combination of a vertical code and a horizontal code (order-"
"independent):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/justification_codes.md:13
msgid "Vertical: **T** (Top), **M** (Middle), **B** (Bottom)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/justification_codes.md:14
msgid "Horizontal: **L** (Left), **C** (Centre), **R** (Right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/justification_codes.md:16
msgid "For example, `\"TL\"` means **T**op **L**eft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/justification_codes.md:18
msgid ""
"The possible nine justification codes are visualized in the sketch below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/justification_codes.md:22
#: ../../../techref/justification_codes.md:73
#: ../../../techref/justification_codes.md:100
msgid "<IPython.core.display.Image object>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/justification_codes.md:68
msgid ""
"For a non-rectangular geographic basemap, the justification codes refer to "
"the invisible, rectangular map bounding box:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/justification_codes.md:94
msgid ""
"Plot embellishments can be abstracted as rectangles. Here, the justification "
"codes are shown exemplary for a colorbar."
msgstr ""
